# aave-mcp configuration.
#
# Wallets:
#   Preferred path is to create `wallets.json` next to this file
#   (see wallets.json.example). It supports multiple wallets with
#   names you can pass to tools as `wallet: "trading"` instead of
#   the raw 0x address.
#
#   For single-wallet setups, you can also use the legacy env var:
# AAVE_DEFAULT_WALLET=0xYourWalletAddress

# Optional path override for wallets.json. Defaults to
# `<connector-root>/wallets.json` (sibling of this file).
# AAVE_WALLETS_FILE=/absolute/path/to/wallets.json

# Per-chain RPC overrides. The server ships with public RPC defaults
# (publicnode.com / chain-native endpoints) that work without API
# keys but may rate-limit under heavier use. For sustained use point
# these at your own Alchemy / Infura / QuickNode / drpc endpoints.
#
# The env var name is <CHAINNAME>_RPC_URL where <CHAINNAME> is the
# chain key in uppercase. Examples:
# ETHEREUM_RPC_URL=
# ARBITRUM_RPC_URL=
# BASE_RPC_URL=
# OPTIMISM_RPC_URL=
# POLYGON_RPC_URL=
# ZKSYNC_RPC_URL=
# … etc. Run with no overrides for the full list of supported chains.
